From: Roman Kuraev <naoru.desu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:23:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: mark the fbdev GEM mapping as system memory

The fbdev buffer is mapped with msm_gem_get_vaddr and uses the
system-memory deferred drawing helpers. Set FBINFO_VIRTFB to describe
that mapping, as the other DRM system-memory fbdev helpers do.
This avoids the framebuffer address-space warning during console draws.

Signed-off-by: Roman Kuraev <naoru.desu@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c
index fd19995b1..d05234bdd 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c
@@ -132,6 +132,7 @@ int msm_fbdev_driver_fbdev_probe(struct drm_fb_helper *helper,
 	helper->fb = fb;
 
 	fbi->fbops = &msm_fb_ops;
+	fbi->flags |= FBINFO_VIRTFB; /* GEM buffer mapped into system memory */
 
 	drm_fb_helper_fill_info(fbi, helper, sizes);
 
